      "claim": "A 1-benzyl-4-piperidinyl benzamide analog exhibited significant and sustained high brain uptake in mice, supporting the CNS-penetrant character of the benzylpiperidine motif present in the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is donepezil, a well-established CNS-active drug. Direct and close-analog evidence consistently demonstrates brain penetration, high brain/plasma ratios, and high brain uptake, supporting meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No quantitative human CSF or unbound brain-to-plasma ratio is provided in the evidence set, but multiple direct rodent BBB penetration measurements and the known clinical CNS activity of donepezil are sufficient."
  ],
